  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we substitute for $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =(\\frac{81{a}^{8}}{{b}^{2}{c}^{3}})\\cdot (\\frac{{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{81{a}^{8}{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}{b}^{2}{c}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the fraction, group the three variables separately, and apply the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{81{a}^{8}{b}^{7}{c}^{11}}{9{a}^{4}{b}^{2}{c}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{81}{9}\\cdot \\frac{{a}^{8}}{{a}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{{b}^{7}}{{b}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{11}}{{c}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{81}{9}\\cdot {a}^{(8-4)}\\cdot {b}^{(7-2)}\\cdot {c}^{(11-3)} & = \\\\ 9{a}^{4}{b}^{5}{c}^{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
